WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.000
With the deep blue base ready, place four mint-colored dabs using a 220 px brush at 50% opacity.

00:10.000 --> 00:20.000
Open the color panel, enter pale purple #B49CFF in HEX, and apply it.

00:20.000 --> 00:30.000
Keep the brush at 220 px and 50% opacity. Add the first pale purple dab beside the mint ones.

00:30.000 --> 00:40.000
Add two more pale purple dabs, offset from the mint group.

00:40.000 --> 00:50.000
Change the color to warm white #FFF1CC.

00:50.000 --> 01:00.000
For the main light, set the brush to 260 px and 75% opacity.

01:00.000 --> 01:10.000
Place a larger, brighter warm light in the upper left.

01:10.000 --> 01:20.000
Reduce the brush to 32 px and raise opacity to 100% for the small stars.

01:20.000 --> 01:30.000
Use very short strokes to add small stars in the darker areas.

01:30.000 --> 01:44.000
Add five small stars in total, leaving deep blue gaps between the larger lights.

01:44.000 --> 01:52.500
Hide the toolbar to view the complete night-glow study.
